# Read by Cloudflare when it builds the asset manifest, exactly like _headers:
# what is listed here is never uploaded and never served.
#
# .DS_Store is the reason this file exists. Finder writes one into public/ the
# moment anyone opens the folder, the build copies it to dist/client, and the
# deploy publishes it — https://sfsymbols.terryhu.workers.dev/.DS_Store answered
# 200 once. Deleting the file only fixes it until the next time someone looks at
# the directory; this fixes it for good.
#
# Three files in dist/client are served and stay that way. Listing this file
# here was tried and does not work — wrangler publishes it regardless — and
# `_headers` and `.vite/manifest.json` must not be listed at all: the first is
# what puts the immutable cache on /symbols/*, the second is the runtime asset
# manifest. None of the three says anything that is not already public.
.DS_Store
